      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَرِقَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَرِقٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, (Msb,) <i>A thing stolen;</i>
(Mgh, Msb;) and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُرَاقَةٌ</span></b> ; [pl. of the latter
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُرَاقَاتٌ</span>;] whence the saying <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِنْدَهُ سُرَاقَاتُ الشِّعْرِ</span>
[<i>He has stolen things of poetry</i> or <i>verse</i>]. (TA.)

